.TH HD-CONFIG-UPDATE 8 "October 2026" "hd-base" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-config-update \- add a key to the hyprdebian configuration or replace its value
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-config-update
.I key
.RI [ json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-config-update
sets
.I key
in the JSON object in
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
to the JSON value
.IR json .
When the key is not there yet, it is added; when it is, its old value is
replaced as a whole.
The other keys stay as they are.
See
.BR hd-config (7)
for how the configuration is used.
.PP
Without
.IR json ,
the value is read from standard input.
.PP
When
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
does not exist yet, it is made, and
.I /etc/hyprdebian
with it.
The file is written with mode 0644.
.PP
Run it as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ,\  \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.TP
.I key
The key in the configuration, usually the name of the package whose settings
it holds. It may not be empty.
.TP
.I json
The value, as JSON text: an object, an array, a string in double quotes, a
number,
.BR true ,
.B false
or
.BR null .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the configuration was written, 1 on an error, 2 on wrong arguments.
On an error the file is left as it was.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set the settings of hd-example:
.PP
.RS
hd-config-update hd-example '{"enabled": true, "port": 8080}'
.RE
.PP
Set a string; the double quotes are part of the JSON:
.PP
.RS
hd-config-update hostname '"repo.example"'
.RE
.PP
Read the value from a file:
.PP
.RS
hd-config-update hd-example < settings.json
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-config (7),
.BR hd-config-remove (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
